.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-hardware-specs
command displays basic hardware specs regarding the BIOS, motherboard,
CPUs, and memory on the terminal.  Information is retrieved using
dmidecode and displayed in standard format.  To utilize the information
in a program, the output must be parsed.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

